Repair the complete TypeScript source below and return one corrected complete source file.

Export `StyleBundle` and `makeReadingLayoutStyles`. The function accepts an optional CSS class prefix, defaulting to `reading`. A valid prefix starts with an ASCII letter or underscore and then contains only ASCII letters, digits, underscores, or hyphens; invalid or empty prefixes cause `TypeError`. Return a newly allocated frozen object with `container`, `text`, and `combined` strings.

The exact CSS rules, without extra whitespace, are:
- container: `.<prefix>-split{display:flex;flex-direction:row}.<prefix>-split>section{width:50%}`
- text: `.<prefix>-text h2{color:#273469;font-size:42px;font-weight:700}.<prefix>-text p{font-size:15px;color:rgba(39,52,105,0.72);font-weight:400;padding-right:96px;margin-top:18px}`
- combined is container followed immediately by text.

The `>section` selector is important: nested sections must not receive the width rule. Inputs are strings and must not be transformed.

Known-bad source:

export interface StyleBundle {
  readonly container: string;
  readonly text: string;
  readonly combined: string;
}

export function makeReadingLayoutStyles(prefix = "reading"): StyleBundle {
  if (!/^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/.test(prefix)) throw new TypeError("Invalid CSS class prefix");
  const container = `.${prefix}-split{display:flex;flex-direction:row}.${prefix}-split section{width:50%}`;
  const text = `.${prefix}-text h2{color:#273469;font-size:42px;font-weight:700}.${prefix}-text p{font-size:15px;color:rgba(39,52,105,0.72);font-weight:400;padding-right:96px;margin-top:18px}`;
  return Object.freeze({ container, text, combined: container + text });
}

